# Deskflow Remote Server (10.1.1.22)

## Host

| | |
|---|---|
| IP | `10.1.1.22` |
| Hostname | `DESKTOP-U00QJVN` |
| WinRM / remoting user | `DESKTOP-U00QJVN\mike` |
| Interactive desktop / Stream Deck user | `micha` |

Stream Deck and Elgato profile data live under **`micha`**, not `mike`. Install plugins and inspect Stream Deck paths for `micha`.

## Credentials

- Cred file: `%USERPROFILE%\.deskflow-remote-10.1.1.22.cred` (Export-Clixml / DPAPI for this Windows user)
- **Never commit** the `.cred` file or paste passwords into the repo/chat logs
- A null/empty import causes interactive password prompts — treat that as broken and re-save

## How agents must remoting

- Always use [`scripts/Invoke-RemoteServer.ps1`](scripts/Invoke-RemoteServer.ps1)
- **Never** call `Get-Credential` in agent sessions (no interactive UI)
- Re-save credentials only via [`scripts/Save-RemoteServerCred.ps1`](scripts/Save-RemoteServerCred.ps1) after a validated username/password round-trip (user runs this interactively once)

```powershell
.\scripts\Invoke-RemoteServer.ps1 { hostname; whoami }
.\scripts\Save-RemoteServerCred.ps1   # interactive, user only
```

## Key remote paths

| What | Path |
|---|---|
| Deskflow install | `C:\Program Files\Deskflow\` |
| Stream Deck plugins (`micha`) | `C:\Users\micha\AppData\Roaming\Elgato\StreamDeck\Plugins\` |
| Stream Deck profiles (`micha`) | `C:\Users\micha\AppData\Roaming\Elgato\StreamDeck\ProfilesV3\` |
